# Backend configuration.#
# Copy to .env in this folder to configure `docker compose up` run FROM HERE. Running the
# root stack instead reads the repo-root .env, not this one — Compose only picks up the
# .env next to the file it was invoked with. Same variable names either way.

# Port the HTTP server listens on.
PORT=3000

# Directory for saved screenshots. Shared with the reader service, which writes them
# there; this process serves them. In Docker it is the mounted volume.
STORAGE_DIR=/app/local-storage

# --- Browser access (the bundled frontend) ---
# Comma-separated origins allowed to call this API from a browser; `*` allows any.
# Empty disables CORS, which is the default: this service has no authentication, so a
# permissive default would let any page the user visits drive their reader.
# CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173

# --- Reader service (crawling) ---
# The service that owns the browser. Unset and GET /<url> reports 503 "not configured".
# Inside the compose network: http://reader:3001
# READER_URL=http://localhost:3001
# Optional shared secret; must match READER_API_KEY on that service.
# READER_API_KEY=

# --- Segmenter service (token counting and chunking) ---
# Unset and /v1/segment reports 503 "not configured", and /v1/embeddings cannot chunk.
# Inside the compose network: http://segmenter:3002
# SEGMENTER_URL=http://localhost:3002
# SEGMENTER_API_KEY=

# --- Web search ---
# A self-hosted SearXNG instance. Leave unset and /v1/search reports 503 "not configured".
# Its JSON API must be enabled (see services/searxng/settings.yml).
# Inside the compose network: http://searxng:8080
# SEARXNG_URL=http://localhost:8080

# --- Model services (embeddings + reranking) ---
# FastAPI services under services/. Unset means /v1/embeddings and /v1/rerank return 503.
# Inside the compose network: http://embeddings:8000 and http://reranker:8000
# Both listen on 8000 and publish no host port by default, so running the backend
# outside compose needs a published port first (add one to their compose files).
# EMBEDDINGS_URL=http://embeddings:8000
# RERANKER_URL=http://reranker:8000
# Optional shared secret; must match INFERENCE_API_KEY on those services.
# INFERENCE_API_KEY=

# --- Optional database (crawl cache) ---
# Postgres connection for Prisma. Leave unset and the service runs standalone with
# caching disabled — nothing else changes.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host:5432/database

# Direct (non-pooled) connection used only for migrations. Set this when DATABASE_URL
# points at a connection pooler, such as Supabase's on port 6543.
# DIRECT_URL=postgresql://user:password@host:5432/database

# How long a cached crawl stays fresh.
# CACHE_TTL_SECONDS=3600
